  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Alaska has $170M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Obligations fell 96.4% year over year. Contracting activity so far includes 814 awards with an average award size of $209K. Federal buying in Alaska is much lower this fiscal year compared with recent history: FY26 obligations were $4.7B, FY25 were $4B, FY24 were $3.9B, FY23 were $3.9B, and FY22 were $3.3B. The Department of Homeland Security is the largest buying agency in FY2027 to date with $141M in obligations, followed by the Department of Health and Human Services with $14.8M and the Department of Agriculture with $11.2M. GILBANE FEDERAL is the largest contractor in FY2027 to date with $114M in obligations. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is the largest industry by obligations in FY2027 to date with $120M, followed by Security Guards and Patrol Services with $32.1M. The current-year totals are partial. All figures are contract obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated is federal spending in Alaska right now?",
        "body": "The FY2027 to date total is $170M, concentrated heavily in a few buyers and industries. The Department of Homeland Security accounts for $141M of that total. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction accounts for $120M of obligations, showing strong concentration by industry."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which sectors and vendors dominate FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "Commercial and Institutional Building Construction and Security Guards and Patrol Services are the top sectors with $120M and $32.1M respectively. GILBANE FEDERAL leads vendors with $114M, followed by TRAILBOSS ENTERPRISES, INC. with $16.1M and BERING STRAITS PROFESSIONAL SERVICES, LLC with $12.3M."
      }
    ]
  },
