      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Alaska?",
      "a": "Alaska received $170M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The state recorded 814 awards with an average award size of $209K. FY26 obligations were $4.7B and prior fiscal years ranged from $3.3B to $4B."
